      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PROTEGE (5) lines up here off a comfortable win at Murray Bridge Straight after jumping from box 3 (16.85). Patchy beginner but with a good start can overcome the draw. Recorded one of the quickest times on the card in scoring last start. Has hit winning form and can go on with it. ZIPPING BELUGA (1) stalked the lead after a clean break from the tricky draw then burst clear to score (17.38) at Murray Bridge Straight in a TG1-4W over 300m. Has performed well from this box with a win and four minor placings to his name from 10 starts. Leading chance again. PINK POPPY CLUB (2) was unfancied latest when jumping from this same draw but belied the odds to place (23.17) over 400m at this track in a Grade 6. Has good early burn and drawn to be prominent early off a low draw. This tougher but looks a leading chance again. ONCE A DIVA (8) was out of the money at this circuit last start but can make amends.",
